content.text:
Now improve hands. Current hand function places root and fingers toward +z (stock side). For right hand gripping pistol grip, fingers wrap front side of grip (toward -z?) Actually grip is at z=0.055, hand should be around z=0.06, fingers wrap the front (negative z) of grip. But from camera behind, we see back of hand. Let's craft hand with palm box and four fingers curling toward -z (front) over the grip.

Hand geometry design in local space:
- Palm: 0.07 wide, 0.10 tall, 0.09 deep at 0,0,0.
- Fingers: 4 small boxes at x offsets across width? In a grip, fingers wrap around the front, so they'd be at z=-0.05, spread in y (stacked vertically) maybe. For a hand holding a rifle grip, fingers stack vertically along the grip front. Actually fingers wrap horizontally around the grip, each finger at different height. So 3-4 boxes at y offsets, z=-0.04, depth 0.04, with slight x spread.
- Thumb on left/right upper side.

Let me rewrite hand:
```
function hand(parent, side=1){
  const g = new THREE.Group();
  g.position.set(side*0.03, -0.108, side>0? 0.06 : -0.40);
  parent.add(g);
  // palm
  box(0.07,0.105,0.09, 0,0,0.01, glove,g,[0.08,0,0]);
  // knuckle pad
  box(0.074,0.032,0.085, 0,0.032,-0.012, glovePad,g,[0.08,0,0]);
  // fingers wrapping forward (-z) around grip
  for(i=0..3) box(0.06,0.022,0.045, 0, 0.038-i*0.026, -0.045, glovePad, g, [0.05,0,0]);
  // thumb along inner side
  box(0.026,0.075,0.03, side*-0.04, 0.028, -0.01, glove, g, [0.12,0,side*-0.5]);
  // cuff
  box(0.082,0.085,0.12, 0,-0.04,0.105, sleeve, g, [0.16,0,0]);
  return g;
}
```
Then right hand position (0.0,-0.11,0.06), left hand at handguard (-0.005,-0.075,-0.43) with wrist angled. But hand function positions root; for left hand, after creation we can reposition and rotate. The left hand fingers should wrap around handguard. We can set off.position and off.rotation.x? Perhaps rotate z by +0.5 for support angle. Support hand under the handguard, palm facing up-ish. Our hand model viewed from above could still look okay with fingers at -z.

Actually from player's view, the support hand on the handguard is mostly hidden by the handguard except the fingers wrapping around the left side. The current placement (-0.035,-0.105,-0.36) is under the receiver near magazine, not handguard. Better -0.045,-0.05,-0.42 with rotation z maybe 0.3 (to bring palm under). Hmm, rotation z tilts.

Larger visual improvement may be sleeves: add forearms extending back toward camera at both hands. Right forearm from grip toward bottom-right; left forearm from handguard toward bottom-left/center. That frames the gun and adds body presence.

Right now sleeve box only 0.13 long at z+0.11 — small. Make forearm longer 0.24 and angled, positioned to extend toward camera, e.g., position (0.01,-0.08,0.19), rotation x 0.35 so it slopes. It may intrude at bottom. Since weapon base positioned right/down, right forearm would go off-screen bottom right — good.

Left forearm extends from handguard down-left toward camera: local in hand group maybe position (side*0.01,-0.07,0.16). But hand group at y -0.05,z -0.42 so forearm extends toward z=-0.26 below handguard — visible along bottom of gun. Good.

Let's rewrite hand with forearm inside, longer.

Also add glove index finger along trigger guard? Not needed.

Then add some more model detail:
- Stock: add butt pad (dark rubber) and cheek riser; sling loop.
- Magazine: add baseplate and witness ribs.
- Add bolt catch, selector switch, takedown pins as small steel cylinders on side.
- Add front/rear flip sights maybe.
- Add QD sling mount.

Small steel details catch light and add realism. But don't overdo.

Also reduce weapon yaw from 0.42 to 0.34 and scale 0.72 maybe.

Let's edit hand function first.

